      "text": "3396.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation and Answer:**\n\nTo find the product of 91 and 36, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break Down the Numbers:**\n   - 91 can be expressed as 90 + 1.\n   - 36 can be expressed as 30 + 6.\n\n2. **Multiply Each Part Separately:**\n   - Multiply 90 by 30: 90 \u00d7 30 = 2700.\n   - Multiply 90 by 6: 90 \u00d7 6 = 540.\n   - Multiply 1 by 30: 1 \u00d7 30 = 30.\n   - Multiply 1 by 6: 1 \u00d7 6 = 6.\n\n3. **Add All the Products Together:**\n   - 2700 + 540 + 30 + 6 = 3276.\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 91 and 36 is 3276.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **30** and **75**, follow these simple steps:\n\n1. **Multiply the two numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   30 \\times 75\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   30 \\times 75 = 2250\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2250}\n\\]",
