      "text": "7769.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **84** and **64**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 84 by 60:**\n   \n   \\[\n   84 \\times 60 = 5040\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 84 by 4:**\n   \n   \\[\n   84 \\times 4 = 336\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the two results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   5040 + 336 = 5376\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of **84** and **64** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5376}\n\\]",
