      "index": 0,
      "text": "9,371 + 128 = 9,499.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try a different approach.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 86 by 60, which equals 5,160.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 86 by 8, giving me 688.\n\nFinally, I'll add those two results together: 5,160 + 688 = 5,848.\n\nYes, that makes more sense. So, the correct product of 86 and 68 is 5,848.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **28** and **79**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 28 by 70:**\n   \n   \\[\n   28 \\times 70 = 1,960\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 28 by 9:**\n   \n   \\[\n   28 \\times 9 = 252\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the two results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1,960 + 252 = 2,212\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of **28** and **79** is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2,\\!212}\n\\]",
